IMPORT prelude

-- Free Trade Zones Act 1966 (Singapore) -- what may be done with goods in a free trade zone and the Director-General's permission for
-- manufacture and dutiable manipulation (ss 5, 6), retail trade, use of unpaid-duty goods and entry into a zone (ss 8, 9, 10) and the
-- Part 2 penalties (s 10A); the FTZ operator licence (s 14A) and regulatory action against a licensee (s 14P); who a cargo handler
-- tells about suspect goods (ss 14J, 14M); obstruction of customs officers (s 14Z); officers of bodies corporate (s 23(1)); appeals
-- (s 18(2)); and composition (s 23A).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/FTZA1966.txt. The cover says it
-- "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021", but the body carries later annotations: Act 33 of 2023 (in force
-- in stages, 1 March 2024 and 25 November 2024) and Act 24 of 2024 (wef 14 November 2024). The latest date annotated is 25/11/2024.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 7 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the rules a trader, zone operator, cargo
-- handler or shipping agent actually meets. Not encoded: the declaration of zones (s 3), delegation (s 4), the rate and valuation
-- date of customs duty (s 7), the licence application and conditions (ss 14B-14E), directions and reports (ss 14F, 14I, 14K, 14L),
-- shipping and air cargo agent information duties (ss 14N, 14O) beyond their penalty, enforcement powers (ss 14Q-14X), false
-- statements (s 14Y), secrecy (s 16A), service (s 18A), the burden of proof (s 20), and regulations (s 24).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Free Trade Zones Act 1966 -- zones`

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the greater of` MEANS IF a >= b THEN a ELSE b

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lower of` MEANS IF a <= b THEN a ELSE b

§§ `5 -- goods in a free trade zone`

-- s 5(1): "Goods of any description, except such as are specifically and absolutely prohibited by any written law, may be brought
-- into a free trade zone."
-- s 5(2)(b): goods may, "unless otherwise directed by the licensed FTZ operator", be stored, sold, exhibited, broken up, repacked,
-- assembled ... or otherwise manipulated, or be manufactured "in accordance with the provisions of this Act".
-- s 5(4): s 5(2)(b) does not apply to goods prescribed by the Minister by Gazette notification, "save that such prescribed goods may
-- be stored ... for the purpose of transhipment or survey and repacking before removal into customs territory", survey and repacking
-- only "with the prior permission of a senior officer of customs".
DECLARE Handling IS ONE OF
    `storage for transhipment`
    `survey and repacking`
    `sale or exhibition`
    `repacking or sorting`

GIVEN `absolutely prohibited by written law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the goods may be brought into the zone` IF
    NOT `absolutely prohibited by written law`

GIVEN `the handling` IS A Handling, `the goods are prescribed under s 5(4)` IS A BOOLEAN, `the operator directed otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `a senior officer permitted it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the handling is permitted under s 5` IF
    IF `the goods are prescribed under s 5(4)`
    THEN CONSIDER `the handling`
         WHEN `storage for transhipment` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `survey and repacking` THEN `a senior officer permitted it`
         OTHERWISE FALSE
    ELSE NOT `the operator directed otherwise`

§§ `6 -- manipulation and manufacture need the Director-General's permission`

-- s 6(1): any person who intends to "(a) assemble, mix or otherwise manipulate any goods for entry into customs territory, where any
-- goods or materials used ... are dutiable goods; (b) manufacture any goods" must give written notice and "obtain the
-- Director-General's prior written permission". s 6(2): granted or withheld "as the Director-General in his discretion shall think fit".
-- s 2: "manufacture" means converting materials into a new product "whereby a change in tariff classification has been effected".
GIVEN `manufactures goods` IS A BOOLEAN, `manipulates goods` IS A BOOLEAN, `for entry into customs territory` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `uses dutiable goods or materials` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `prior written permission is needed` IF
        `manufactures goods`
    OR  (`manipulates goods` AND `for entry into customs territory` AND `uses dutiable goods or materials`)

§§ `8, 9, 10 -- retail trade, unpaid-duty goods, entry`

-- s 8(1): "No retail trade shall be conducted within a free trade zone unless authorised in writing by the licensed FTZ operator".
-- s 9: a person "who knows or has reason to believe" that customs duty or tax on dutiable or taxable goods in a zone has not been paid
-- "must not use or consume the goods, unless the customs duty and tax on the goods are paid ... before the use or consumption".
-- s 10(1): no person may "enter or reside in a free trade zone without the permission of the licensed FTZ operator"; (2) "Despite any
-- permission granted by the licensed FTZ operator", the Director-General may by written order prohibit a person from entering.
GIVEN `conducts retail trade in the zone` IS A BOOLEAN, `authorised in writing by the operator` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the retail trade is an offence` IF
    `conducts retail trade in the zone` AND (NOT `authorised in writing by the operator`)

GIVEN `knows or has reason to believe duty or tax is unpaid` IS A BOOLEAN, `uses or consumes the goods` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `duty and tax paid before use` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the use is an offence under s 9` IF
    `knows or has reason to believe duty or tax is unpaid` AND `uses or consumes the goods` AND (NOT `duty and tax paid before use`)

GIVEN `has the operator's permission` IS A BOOLEAN, `is under a Director-General's prohibition order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person may enter or reside in the zone` IF
    `has the operator's permission` AND (NOT `is under a Director-General's prohibition order`)

§§ `10A -- penalties under Part 2`

-- s 10A(1): failing to comply with an operator's direction under s 5(2), or with s 6(1): "a fine not exceeding the greater of ...
-- (i) $10,000; (ii) the sum total of the customs duty and tax on the goods ... or (b) imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12 months,
-- or to both". (2) s 8: fine not exceeding $10,000. (3) s 9: as (1). (4) s 10(1) or a s 10(2) order: fine not exceeding $5,000.
DECLARE PartTwoOffence IS ONE OF
    `ignoring an operator's direction under s 5(2)`
    `manufacturing without permission under s 6(1)`
    `unauthorised retail trade under s 8`
    `using unpaid-duty goods under s 9`
    `unauthorised entry under s 10`

GIVEN `the offence` IS A PartTwoOffence, `duty and tax on the goods` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine under s 10A` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `unauthorised retail trade under s 8` THEN 10000
    WHEN `unauthorised entry under s 10` THEN 5000
    OTHERWISE `the greater of` 10000 `duty and tax on the goods`

GIVEN `the offence` IS A PartTwoOffence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum months of imprisonment under s 10A` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `unauthorised retail trade under s 8` THEN 0
    WHEN `unauthorised entry under s 10` THEN 0
    OTHERWISE 12

§§ `14A, 14P -- the operator licence and regulatory action`

-- s 14A(1): "A person must not administer, maintain or operate a free trade zone unless the person is authorised to do so by an FTZ
-- operator licence"; (2) fine not exceeding $10,000. s 14C(2): "An FTZ operator licence is not transferrable."
GIVEN `operates a free trade zone` IS A BOOLEAN, `holds an FTZ operator licence for it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `operating the zone is an offence` IF
    `operates a free trade zone` AND (NOT `holds an FTZ operator licence for it`)

-- s 14P(1): the Director-General may suspend or revoke "(without any compensation)" if satisfied that (a) the licensee contravened a
-- licence condition or a non-offence provision; (b) the application was false or misleading or the licence obtained by fraud;
-- (c) the licensee "is convicted of any offence under this Act committed during the term of the licence"; or (d) "the public interest
-- or national security of Singapore requires".
-- s 14P(2)(d): "for any contravention under subsection (1)(a)", a financial penalty "not exceeding $10,000".
-- s 14P(3)(c): the notice must give a time "being not less than 14 days after the date of service" for written representations.
-- s 14P(8): if the licence ceases after notice, the Director-General may still take the action in "(2)(a) and (d)" (censure, financial
-- penalty) against the former licensee.
DECLARE Ground IS ONE OF
    `breach of a licence condition`
    `false or misleading application`
    `conviction for an offence under this Act during the licence`
    `conviction for an offence before the licence`
    `public interest or national security`
    `none of these`

DECLARE Action IS ONE OF
    `suspension or revocation`
    `censure`
    `financial penalty`

GIVEN `the ground` IS A Ground
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the ground supports suspension or revocation` IF
    CONSIDER `the ground`
    WHEN `conviction for an offence before the licence` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `none of these` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the ground` IS A Ground, `the action` IS A Action, `penalty amount` IS A NUMBER, `days allowed for representations` IS A NUMBER,
      `the licence is still in force` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the regulatory action is open to the Director-General` IF
        `the ground supports suspension or revocation` `the ground`
    AND `days allowed for representations` >= 14
    AND CONSIDER `the action`
        WHEN `suspension or revocation` THEN `the licence is still in force`
        WHEN `censure` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `financial penalty` THEN
            (`the ground` EQUALS `breach of a licence condition`) AND `penalty amount` <= 10000

§§ `14J, 14M -- disclosing suspect goods`

-- s 14J(1): a licensed FTZ operator with "reason to suspect" goods in its or a cargo handler's control are moved or manufactured "in
-- contravention of this Act or any other written law" must disclose the suspicion to the Director-General; (2) $5,000.
-- s 14M(2): where the cargo handler "is also the licensed FTZ operator", it discloses to the Director-General under s 14J(1); (3)
-- where it "is not the licensed FTZ operator", it must disclose "to the licensed FTZ operator of the relevant free trade zone"; (4)
-- failure under (3) without reasonable excuse: $5,000.
DECLARE Recipient IS ONE OF
    `the Director-General`
    `the licensed FTZ operator`
    `no one`

GIVEN `has reason to suspect a contravention` IS A BOOLEAN, `is the licensed FTZ operator` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Recipient
`the cargo handler must disclose to` MEANS
    IF `has reason to suspect a contravention`
    THEN IF `is the licensed FTZ operator`
         THEN `the Director-General`
         ELSE `the licensed FTZ operator`
    ELSE `no one`

§§ `14Z -- assaulting or obstructing officers`

-- s 14Z: assaulting or obstructing an officer, rescuing detained goods, staving packages, resisting arrest or escaping: "(e) on
-- conviction to a fine not exceeding $10,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 18 months or to both; and (f) in the case of
-- a second or subsequent conviction, to a fine not exceeding $20,000 and to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 3 years."
GIVEN `previous convictions under s 14Z` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 14Z maximum fine` MEANS IF `previous convictions under s 14Z` >= 1 THEN 20000 ELSE 10000

GIVEN `previous convictions under s 14Z` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 14Z maximum months of imprisonment` MEANS IF `previous convictions under s 14Z` >= 1 THEN 36 ELSE 18

§§ `23(1) -- officers of bodies of persons`

-- s 23(1): where a company, firm, society or other body commits an offence, a director, manager, secretary or similar officer or a
-- partner "shall be deemed to be guilty of that offence, unless he proves that the offence was committed without his consent or
-- connivance and that he exercised all such diligence to prevent the commission of the offence as he ought to have exercised".
GIVEN `the body committed an offence` IS A BOOLEAN, `was a director, manager, secretary or partner` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `proves no consent or connivance` IS A BOOLEAN, `proves due diligence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer is deemed guilty` IF
        `the body committed an offence` AND `was a director, manager, secretary or partner`
    AND (NOT (`proves no consent or connivance` AND `proves due diligence`))

§§ `18(2) -- an appeal does not suspend the decision`

-- s 18(1): any person aggrieved by a decision of a licensed FTZ operator or the Director-General "may appeal to the Minister".
-- (2): an appeal "does not affect the operation of the decision ... and unless otherwise directed by the Minister, the decision
-- appealed against must be complied with until the determination of the appeal".
GIVEN `an appeal is pending` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Minister directed otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the decision must be complied with now` IF
    (NOT `an appeal is pending`) OR (NOT `the Minister directed otherwise`)

§§ `23A -- composition`

-- s 23A(1): the Director-General may compound an offence "prescribed as a compoundable offence" by collecting "a sum not exceeding the
-- lower of ... (a) one half of the amount of the maximum fine that is prescribed for the offence; (b) $5,000". (2) no further
-- proceedings once paid.
GIVEN `prescribed as compoundable` IS A BOOLEAN, `maximum fine for the offence` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum composition sum` MEANS
    IF `prescribed as compoundable`
    THEN `the lower of` (`maximum fine for the offence` / 2) 5000
    ELSE 0
